{"id":"h6-11-p11","title":"Design a live leaderboard","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: requirements, API, Redis sorted sets, windows, sharding, ties, friends board. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"requirements","title":"Requirements","html":"<p><strong>A live leaderboard shows the top players by score and each player's own rank, updated as scores change.</strong> Think of a game ranking (Fortnite, Dream11 contests, Clash of Clans), a coding contest standings board, or a fitness-app weekly challenge. The challenge: ranking millions of players in real time without sorting them on every request.</p>\n<p><strong>Functional requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Submit or update a score for a user.</li>\n<li>Get the top N (for example top 100) of a leaderboard.</li>\n<li>Get a user's rank and score, and the players around them (rank +/- 5).</li>\n<li>Multiple boards: global, per region, per friends, per time window (daily, weekly, all-time).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Non-functional requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read p99 under 50 ms; score update visible within 1 s.</li>\n<li>Scale: 50M players, 20k score updates/s at peak, 100k leaderboard reads/s.</li>\n<li>Correct ranks (ties handled deterministically); durable scores.</li>\n<li>Highly available; a stale leaderboard for a few seconds is acceptable.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 488.8 130\" width=\"488.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scores in, ranks out\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M303.2 34 L359.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M303.2 34 L359.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M303.2 96 L359.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M303.2 96 L359.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Game server</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Player</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"237.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Score API</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"237.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Leaderboard API</text><rect x=\"359.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"418\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Ranking store</text></svg><figcaption>Scores in, ranks out</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Choose an in-memory sorted structure (Redis sorted set) rather than <code>SELECT ... ORDER BY score DESC</code> on a SQL table. SQL needs an index scan and a count to get a rank, O(n) for the count unless carefully indexed, which dies at tens of millions of rows. Redis gives O(log n) for both update and rank. Reversible: the sorted set is a derived view of a durable score table.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A scoreboard where cards slide into the correct slot as soon as a team scores, instead of staff re-sorting the whole list every minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Computing rank with <code>COUNT(*) WHERE score > x</code> on every request.</li>\n<li>Ignoring tie-breaking (two players with 1,000 points).</li>\n<li>Not saying what happens when Redis loses data.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"api","title":"API","html":"<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">POST /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/boards/global-weekly/scores</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Authorization: Bearer &#x3C;game-server-token></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"userId\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"u_42\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"delta\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">150</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"eventId\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"e_9981\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }     </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// or \"score\": 8200 for absolute</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"userId\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"u_42\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"score\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">8350</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"rank\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1204551</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">409</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> -> duplicate eventId (already applied; returns the existing result)</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Server-to-server only: never let clients post their own scores (cheating). <code>eventId</code> makes the update idempotent.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">GET /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/boards/global-weekly/top?limit=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">100</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"updatedAt\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"2026-11-09T14:00:02Z\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">      \"entries\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [ { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"rank\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"userId\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"u_7\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"name\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Neo\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"score\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">99120</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">...</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> ] }</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">GET /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/boards/global-weekly/users/u_</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">42</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"rank\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1204551</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"score\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">8350</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"percentile\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">97.6</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">GET /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/boards/global-weekly/users/u_</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">42</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/around?span=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">5</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"entries\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [ {</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">rank</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1204546</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">...</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">...</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, {</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">rank</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1204556</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">...</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">} ] }</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Friends board: <code>GET /v1/boards/global-weekly/friends?userId=u_42</code> returns scores of the user's friends (usually a few hundred) sorted by score.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Redis's own documentation uses the leaderboard as the sorted-set showcase; Dream11 and Fortnite-type games rank millions of players in real time; Google Play Games Services exposes a similar leaderboard API.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A race marshal who reports your position and the runners just ahead and behind.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Accepting scores from client apps.</li>\n<li>Non-idempotent increments, so a retry double-counts.</li>\n<li>Returning the entire leaderboard instead of a page.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"estimates","title":"Estimates","html":"<p>Assume 50M players on the global board, 20k updates/s peak, 100k reads/s.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Quantity</th>\n<th>Calculation</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Sorted-set memory</td>\n<td>each member ~ 60-100 B (skiplist node + dict entry + 8 B score + id)</td>\n<td>50M x ~90 B = ~4.5 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Boards</td>\n<td>global + 30 regions + daily/weekly windows</td>\n<td>about 100 sets, still &#x3C; 20 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Redis capacity</td>\n<td>one instance ~ 80-100k simple ops/s; ZADD/ZRANK are O(log n), ~20 comparisons at 50M</td>\n<td>20k writes + 100k reads needs read replicas</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Top-N response</td>\n<td>100 entries x 60 B</td>\n<td>6 KB, cacheable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Durable store</td>\n<td>50M rows x 100 B per board</td>\n<td>~5 GB per board</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Write log</td>\n<td>20k/s x 100 B</td>\n<td>2 MB/s = 170 GB/day (retain 7 days in Kafka)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Memory is modest, so a single Redis shard can hold the whole board; the pressure is op rate and fault tolerance, not size.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry example.</strong> Redis sorted sets store ~10M-member sets comfortably in a few GB; teams report millisecond ZRANK on tens of millions.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> The whole scoreboard fits on one wall; the issue is how many people are reading it at once.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sharding at 5 GB when one node suffices.</li>\n<li>Forgetting that 100k reads/s must be spread across replicas.</li>\n<li>Counting only storage and not op rate.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"high-level-design","title":"High-level design","html":"<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 951.1999999999999 130\" width=\"951.1999999999999\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Update path\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M288.8 65 L344.8 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M288.8 65 L344.8 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M512.8 65 L568.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M512.8 65 L568.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M700.8 34 L756.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M700.8 34 L756.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M512.8 65 L568.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M512.8 65 L568.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M700.8 96 L756.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M700.8 96 L756.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Game server</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Score service</text><rect x=\"344.8\" y=\"43\" width=\"168\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"428.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kafka (score events)</text><rect x=\"568.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"634.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Ranking updater</text><rect x=\"568.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"634.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Persister</text><rect x=\"756.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"182.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"848\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis sorted set</text><rect x=\"756.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"182.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"848\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">SQL / Cassandra scores</text></svg><figcaption>Update path</figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 670.8 130\" width=\"670.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Read path\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 65 L346 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 65 L346 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M478 34 L534 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M478 34 L534 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 65 L346 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 65 L346 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Player</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Leaderboard API</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"412\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Top-N cache</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"412\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Profile service</text><rect x=\"534\" y=\"43\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"596.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis replicas</text></svg><figcaption>Read path</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Components:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Score service</strong>: authenticates the game server, validates (max delta per event), dedupes by <code>eventId</code> (Redis <code>SET NX</code> with 24 h TTL), publishes to Kafka.</li>\n<li><strong>Kafka</strong>, partitioned by <code>userId</code>, preserves per-user order.</li>\n<li><strong>Ranking updater</strong>: applies <code>ZINCRBY board userId delta</code> (or <code>ZADD GT</code> for best-score boards) to Redis.</li>\n<li><strong>Redis primary + 2 replicas</strong> per board shard; reads go to replicas.</li>\n<li><strong>Persister</strong>: writes the durable score table (source of truth) and snapshots.</li>\n<li><strong>Top-N cache</strong>: top 100 recomputed every 1 s and cached in the app (it changes slowly at the top).</li>\n<li><strong>Profile service</strong>: joins <code>userId</code> to display name and avatar at read time.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity: Redis as derived, not primary.</strong> Why: durable table plus Kafka allows rebuilding the sorted set (<code>ZADD</code> bulk load of 50M takes a few minutes). Alternative: Redis as the only store with AOF; faster to build but riskier. Breaks if a failover loses recent writes; replay the last minutes from Kafka. Reversible.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity: tie-breaking.</strong> Redis orders equal scores lexicographically by member, which is arbitrary. For \"first to reach the score wins\", encode <code>score * 2^20 + (MAX_TS - timestamp)</code> into a double (careful: a double has 53 bits of integer precision). That choice is a one-way door for existing data because all stored scores change shape; decide before launch.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Riot, Supercell and Zynga have described leaderboards built on Redis; Discord-like bots use ZSETs; large sites often combine Redis with SQL for durability.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> The scoreboard operator (Redis) works from the official scorer's sheets (SQL); if the board is wiped he can redo it from the sheets.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Not choosing a tie-breaker.</li>\n<li>Floating-point precision for composite scores.</li>\n<li>Reading names from Redis (keep it lean; fetch profile data elsewhere).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"deep-dives","title":"Deep dives","html":"<h3>How the sorted set works</h3>\n<p>A Redis ZSET is a skiplist (ordered by score) plus a hash table (member to score). <code>ZADD</code> and <code>ZRANK</code> are O(log n); <code>ZREVRANGE 0 99</code> is O(log n + 100). Rank is derived from skiplist span counters, no scan.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 726.4000000000001 68\" width=\"726.4000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Operations used\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M194.4 34 L250.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M194.4 34 L250.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M411.20000000000005 34 L467.20000000000005 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M411.20000000000005 34 L467.20000000000005 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"182.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"103.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ZINCRBY board u_42 150</text><rect x=\"250.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"330.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ZREVRANK board u_42</text><rect x=\"467.20000000000005\" y=\"12\" width=\"247.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"590.8000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ZREVRANGE board 0 99 WITHSCORES</text></svg><figcaption>Operations used</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ZADD</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> lb:global:2026w45</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> GT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 8350</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> u_42</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ZREVRANK</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> lb:global:2026w45</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> u_42</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">            # 0-based rank from top</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ZREVRANGE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> lb:global:2026w45</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 99</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> WITHSCORES</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ZREVRANGE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> lb:global:2026w45</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 1204546</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 1204556</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> WITHSCORES</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">   # around me</span></span></code></pre>\n<h3>Time windows</h3>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 763.2 68\" width=\"763.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One sorted set per window\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M317.6 34 L373.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M317.6 34 L373.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M527.2 34 L583.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M527.2 34 L583.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Score event</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"244.39999999999998\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ZINCRBY daily key</text><rect x=\"373.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"450.40000000000003\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ZINCRBY weekly key</text><rect x=\"583.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"168\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"667.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ZINCRBY all-time key</text></svg><figcaption>One sorted set per window</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Keys like <code>lb:global:d:2026-11-09</code> with <code>EXPIRE</code> of 8 days; weekly sets expire after the following week. At window end snapshot the top 1,000 to SQL for history and rewards. Writing to 3 keys triples write ops (60k/s): still fine for a pipeline of batched commands.</p>\n<h3>Scaling past one node</h3>\n<p>When a single set no longer fits or ops exceed limits (hundreds of millions of members, 100k+ writes/s), shard.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 562 130\" width=\"562\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Score-range sharding keeps global rank cheap\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 34 L164 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 34 L164 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M254 65 L310 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M254 65 L310 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M108 96 L164 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 96 L164 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M254 65 L310 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M254 65 L310 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Update</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Rank query</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Router</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"12\" width=\"240\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"430\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Shard by score range</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"74\" width=\"240\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"430\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Count above range + local rank</text></svg><figcaption>Score-range sharding keeps global rank cheap</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Option A, partition by <code>userId</code> hash: updates scale, but global top-N needs merging the top N from each shard (cheap: N x shards) and exact rank needs summing counts across shards (<code>ZCOUNT</code> on each: expensive). Option B, partition by score range: exact rank is <code>sum of sizes of higher shards + local rank</code>, but hot ranges cause imbalance and users migrate shards as scores grow. Pragmatic answer: hash shard plus approximate rank for deep positions (\"top 3%\") and exact rank only for the top 10,000. Decision gravity: sharding scheme is a one-way door.</p>\n<h3>Approximate rank at huge scale</h3>\n<p>Maintain a histogram of scores (for example 1,000 buckets updated with counters). Rank of a score = sum of counts in higher buckets plus interpolation. Error stays under 0.1%, cost O(buckets). Used when nobody cares whether you are 1,204,551st or 1,204,600th.</p>\n<h3>Friends leaderboard</h3>\n<p>Friend lists are small (under a few thousand): fetch the friend ids, <code>ZMSCORE</code>/pipelined <code>ZSCORE</code> for each, sort in the service. Alternative: store a per-user friends ZSET (fan-out on write, expensive for large graphs). Compute on read with a 5-10 s cache.</p>\n<h3>Hot reads and consistency</h3>\n<p>Top 100 is read by everyone: cache in app memory with 1 s TTL (100k reads/s become 1 per second per server). Own-rank read goes to a replica; replication lag of tens of ms means a player might not see their just-submitted score; read-your-writes by returning the new score and rank in the POST response and showing it directly.</p>\n<h3>Persistence and recovery</h3>\n<p>Source of truth: <code>scores(board, user_id, score, updated_at)</code> in Postgres/Cassandra, written from Kafka consumers. Redis with AOF <code>everysec</code> plus replicas; on total loss rebuild from the table in minutes. Idempotent <code>eventId</code> prevents double counts during replay.</p>\n<h3>Anti-cheat</h3>\n<p>Server-authoritative scores only, cap per-event delta, anomaly detection (score jump rate), and a shadow-ban list excluded from top-N queries.</p>\n<p><strong>Production incident patterns.</strong> (1) Redis memory growth because old window keys never expire: metric <code>used_memory</code>, check keys without TTL. (2) A big <code>ZREVRANGE 0 -1</code> blocks the single-threaded Redis; enforce a max page size of 100-1000 and use <code>SLOWLOG</code>. (3) Failover loses the last second of writes; compare Redis against Kafka offsets, replay.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Redis sorted sets, Dream11 contests, Fortnite rankings, and Codeforces-like standings for contests.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Sorting a class by marks: keep a sorted list and slot each new mark in, rather than re-sorting the whole class for each question.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Thinking sharding is mandatory at 50M members.</li>\n<li>Exact global rank across hash shards without saying the cost.</li>\n<li>Letting clients submit scores.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-interviewers-look-for","title":"What interviewers look for","html":"<ul>\n<li>Choosing a sorted structure and explaining O(log n) rank and update.</li>\n<li>Sizing: 50M members is only a few GB.</li>\n<li>Durability story: SQL/Kafka as source of truth, Redis as a rebuildable view.</li>\n<li>Windows, friends boards and tie-breaking handled explicitly.</li>\n<li>Hot-read caching of top N, replicas for reads.</li>\n<li>A believable scale-out path (hash shards plus approximations) and its trade-offs.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Redis sorted set: ZINCRBY/ZADD for updates, ZREVRANK for rank, ZREVRANGE for top N, all O(log n).</li>\n<li>50M members is about 4.5 GB; one primary with replicas covers 20k writes/s and 100k reads/s.</li>\n<li>Scores come from trusted servers with idempotent event ids; Kafka feeds Redis and the durable table.</li>\n<li>Separate keys per window (daily, weekly) with TTLs; snapshot winners to SQL.</li>\n<li>Cache the top 100 for 1 s; neighbours via rank +/- span.</li>\n<li>Shard only when forced, using approximate ranks for deep positions.</li>\n<li>Pick the tie-break encoding before launch; it is hard to change later.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}